/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  THE LIQUID-LIQUID PHASE MAP OF
  tutorials/props/scan/ternary03_lle_water_ethanol_benzene, CAPTURED.

  tests/hunterNash.test.ts read that case's `ternary.csv` and its own header
  called it "the engine's own COMMITTED output".  It is not committed:
  .gitignore sweeps every CSV under tutorials/, so the file exists only where
  somebody has run the witness, and the suite was green by circumstance -- the
  same shape as tests/fixtures/flash01Txy.ts beside it, and found the same day,
  by the GUI bundle's new refusal to inline run outputs rather than by anyone
  reading the test.  A message that calls an untracked artefact "committed" is
  the part worth keeping in mind: the suite was not merely lucky, it stated the
  opposite of the truth about its own subject.

  PROVENANCE.  Produced by the native `choupoProps` of this tree at 058fb70dc
  on 2026-09-21, from that case unmodified; byte-identical to the run output
  then on disk.  `mode lle`, `grid { n 16; }`, `tieStride 4` -- 105 nodes, 18
  tie-lines, which are the numbers the case's OWN golden pins, and which the
  test re-reads from that golden rather than trusting this sentence.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

